  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEAF Colombia Agribusiness Fund (SEAF)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">SEAF Fondo Agronegocios Colombia (SEAF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Colombia):  .USAID/Colombia partners with the Small Enterprise Assistance Fund (SEAF) in support of the Colombia Agribusiness Fund, which promotes licit economic growth in rural and conflict-affected areas of Colombia. FY 2018 funds will foster employment and improve incomes through investments in fast-growing, small and medium-sized enterprises. Over the partnership&apos;s lifetime, USAID/Colombia will invest USD $13 million and leverage up to $50 million in new private sector investments. SEAF will invest in 10-15 Colombian enterprises across the agribusiness value chain, focusing on rural agribusiness firms that have a &quot;double bottom line&quot; (i.e. firms that are seeking both social and financial returns) and estimates the creation of 1,500 jobs in the formal economy. Priority sectors include: cacao, chocolate, produce, animal proteins and animal feed, dairy, aquaculture, organic foods, rubber, and timber.  By partnering with the private sector to scale high-potential companies, this activity advances Colombia&apos;s self-reliance and directly contributes to the USG Mission Objective to improve conditions for inclusive rural economic growth and sustainable development....</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">(Colombia): USAID/Colombia se asocia con el Fondo de Asistencia a Peque&#xf1;as Empresas (SEAF) en apoyo al Fondo Agronegocios de Colombia, que promueve el crecimiento econ&#xf3;mico l&#xed;cito en &#xe1;reas rurales y afectadas por conflictos de Colombia. Los fondos del a&#xf1;o fiscal 2018 fomentar&#xe1;n el empleo y mejorar&#xe1;n los ingresos a trav&#xe9;s de inversiones en peque&#xf1;as y medianas empresas de r&#xe1;pido crecimiento. Durante la vigencia de la asociaci&#xf3;n, USAID/Colombia invertir&#xe1; USD $13 millones y aprovechar&#xe1; hasta $50 millones en nuevas inversiones del sector privado. SEAF invertir&#xe1; en entre 10 y 15 empresas colombianas a lo largo de la cadena de valor de los agronegocios, enfoc&#xe1;ndose en empresas de agronegocios rurales que tienen un &quot;doble resultado&quot; (es decir, empresas que buscan retornos tanto sociales como financieros) y estima la creaci&#xf3;n de 1.500 empleos en la econom&#xed;a formal. Los sectores prioritarios incluyen: cacao, chocolate, productos agr&#xed;colas, prote&#xed;nas y piensos animales, l&#xe1;cteos, acuicultura, alimentos org&#xe1;nicos, caucho y madera.  Al asociarse con el sector privado para escalar empresas de alto potencial, esta actividad promueve la autosuficiencia de Colombia y contribuye directamente al objetivo de la misi&#xf3;n del Gobierno de los Estados Unidos de mejorar las condiciones para el crecimiento econ&#xf3;mico rural inclusivo y el desarrollo sostenible....</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives for Colombia: IMPROVING LIVES:The Colombia Agribusiness Fund will improve the lives of people in the rural, marginalized regions of Colombia by fostering employment and improving incomes through investments in fast-growing, small and medium-sized enterprises..RAISING CAPITAL: Through SEAF, USAID will invest $10 million and serve as a limited partner for the investment fund. With USAID providing the initial capital, the Colombia Agribusiness Fund will improve its ability to raise capital from other investors, including, but not limited to, those with a social/development agenda. It is expected that the Colombia Agribusiness Fund will leverage $18 million in the first fund closure 2016), $12 million in the second fund closure (Jun 2017), and potentially leverage an additional $30.million in the third closure, for a total of $60 million. Any financial returns on USAID&#x2019;s investment funds will be reinvested by SEAF back into rural development in Colombia. TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE:  In addition to capitalizing the Agribusiness Fund, USAID and SEAF will create a technical assistance tool that will serve small and medium-sized enterprises operating in agribusiness value chains in Colombia&#x2019;s rural regions. This tool will help develop an agribusiness network, enhance portfolio company operations, and provide training to employees of portfolio companies, among other activities.</narrative>
  </description>
